Z||000000||overlord||04-12-99||06:52 PM||||whenver my fiero gets warmed up, when i slow down to 50kph or slower, the temperture/oil light comes on...but if i speed up it goes off..also i can turn up the heat and the light will flicker and go out....is this just a faulty light? no engine light ever comes on.    84 fiero s.e.
Z||000001||PaUL||04-12-99||08:18 PM||||Which on is it, the oil or temp lite? From past experience I can tell you the electric fan doesnt come on until the engine is almost boiling over, or until you turn the A/C on. If your oil pressure gauge is reading pressure and your temp gauge says the temmp is ok, I wouldnt worry about it.
Z||000002||overlord||04-12-99||09:48 PM||||well heres the thing, my temperature GAUGE doesnt work at all.<br>the light that comes on is what looks like a combo oil/temp light. im not even sure exactly what it is for but it comes on only when the engine is warmed up..<br>i dont have an oil preasure GUAGE, there is just this light thing.
Z||000003||theogre||04-12-99||10:09 PM||||replace the temp sender. both the light and guage work off one sender unit according to my notes.<p>also hook up a guage, at least a temporary one, for oil presure. no sense taking chances with oil pumps.
Z||000004||overlord||04-13-99||02:23 PM||||thanx theogre.<p>your  help is much appreciated...its certainly a lot cheaper than dragging my fiero down to the local shop for diagnostics.<p>thanx again..
